.TH SOLOIST-DISPLAY 1 "November 2026" "Soloist Display" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
soloist-display \- launch the Soloist now-playing display or its settings
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B soloist-display
.RI [ --settings | --help | --version ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B soloist-display
starts the per-user
.B soloist-display.service
if necessary, waits for its local HTTP server, and opens the display in the default browser using
.BR xdg-open (1).
The display is served at
.IR http://127.0.0.1:8080/ .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --settings
Open the settings interface at
.IR http://127.0.0.1:8080/settings .
.TP
.BR -h , " --help"
Show command usage without starting the service.
.TP
.BR -V , " --version"
Show the installed package version without starting the service.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/soloist-display/config.json
Per-user display settings.
.SH SERVICES
.TP
.B soloist-display.service
The systemd user service hosting the display and audio bridge.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Returns a nonzero status if the user service cannot be started, the HTTP endpoint does not become ready, or opening the browser fails.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B soloist-display
Open the now-playing screen.
.TP
.B soloist-display --settings
Open display settings.
.TP
.B systemctl --user status soloist-display.service
Check service status.
.TP
.B journalctl --user -u soloist-display.service -n 50
Inspect recent service logs.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR journalctl (1),
.BR xdg-open (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Soloist Display contributors.
